  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: North Leigh</p>\r\n<p>Excavations were carried out 1813-1816 and 1910-1911. These investigations identified three building phases: I) late first or early second century, II) late second century, III) early third century.</p>\r\n<p>This was a large villa, with the main courtyard villa building complex measuring ca. 65 by 50 m. More than 60 rooms are arranged around three sides of the courtyard.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "North Leigh Roman villa is a large villa complex located near the River Evenlode. This was a luxurious villa with four bathing suites.",
